      "content": "That's a very specific image. It feels very traditional, very \"old money\" European. But I'm worried we might be missing out on a huge segment of the market. In today's global economy, there's a massive amount of new wealth coming from different backgrounds—Silicon Valley tech moguls, new money in East Asia, or even emerging markets in the Middle East and Africa. \n\nDo you think we should adjust this persona to include more diverse racial or ethnic profiles to stay relevant, or does the \"ultra-premium\" status strictly require sticking to that specific European heritage profile you just described? Why is that specific demographic the \"ideal\" for this level of luxury? Is there any way wealth manifests differently in other cultures that would still",
